'''Aushiri''' (Auxira, Awishira, Vacacocha) is an [[Extinct language|extinct]] [[Zaparoan languages|Zaparoan language]] formerly spoken in [[Peru]]. It was spoken in the area of the tributaries to the right bank of the [[Napo River]], in the [[Escuelacocha]] region.

